                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='16' underline='true'>MTD MoM with Different Days</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Standard Formula</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>MTD MoM = (MTD of current month - MTD of previous month) / MTD of previous month</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Adjustment for Different Number of Days</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>When the number of days in the current month and the previous month are different (e.g., calculating on 3/30 wehn February has only 28 days), the previous month&apos;s MTD is adjusted to a comparable scale:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>MTD of previous month = (Total value of the previous month / total days of the month) * days of the current month</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
